2026-11-10: Version 1.1.0

This release adds support for ENUM types and overloaded routines, fixes
several bugs and standardizes the parameter names of internal functions.

  - Add ENUM object type to get_ddl() and get_dependent_ddl(). Thanks to
    Julien Monticolo for the patch.
  - Qualify enum names with their schema when a schema is given, the
    output no longer depends on the search_path.
  - Fix get_ddl() for overloaded procedures and functions: the DDL of all
    the routines with the given name is returned, a single one can be
    selected by appending its argument types to the name, for example
    'my_function(char, char)'. Thanks to loicmalassis for the report.
  - Fix comments containing a quote in the table DDL. Thanks to Julien
    Monticolo for the patch.
  - Fix setting the default value of boolean transform params. Thanks to
    lilw5 for the patch.
  - Fix error handlers of get_type_ddl() and get_enum_ddl() that were
    referencing nonexistent variables.
  - Standardize the parameter names of internal functions: schema_name
    and <object>_name. The public API keeps the Oracle parameter names.
    Thanks to Julien Monticolo for the report.
  - Fix regression tests and add a GitHub Actions workflow running them
    on PostgreSQL 12 to 19, together with a test of the upgrade from each
    released version (test/upgrade_check.sh).

To upgrade an existing installation run:

    ALTER EXTENSION pg_dbms_metadata UPDATE TO "1.1.0";

